WEBVTT

1
01:00:54.858 --> 01:00:58.858
What are you going to be crazy about on stage?

2
01:00:59.858 --> 01:01:01.858
Tommy, aren't you also celebrating your birthday today?

3
01:01:02.858 --> 01:01:03.858
50, right?

4
01:01:03.858 --> 01:01:04.858
Okay, then let's go again.

5
01:01:06.858 --> 01:01:08.858
Stand up, then we'll go again, okay?

6
01:01:23.858 --> 01:01:32.858
Tommy, you heard you're 50 today, right?

7
01:01:32.858 --> 01:01:33.858
That's true.

8
01:01:33.858 --> 01:01:35.858
Where are you going to treat yourself later?

9
01:01:36.858 --> 01:01:37.858
Just asking.

10
01:01:37.858 --> 01:01:38.858
Me neither.

11
01:01:38.858 --> 01:01:39.858
You neither?

12
01:01:39.858 --> 01:01:40.858
Well, go ahead then.

13
01:01:41.858 --> 01:01:42.858
Do you know why?

14
01:01:42.858 --> 01:01:43.858
What then?

15
01:01:43.858 --> 01:01:44.858
My verse is about that.

16
01:01:44.858 --> 01:01:45.858
Your verse is about that.

17
01:01:45.858 --> 01:01:47.858
Robert, you are a wonderful man.

18
01:01:47.858 --> 01:01:49.858
And Tommy, you too by the way, really.

19
01:01:50.858 --> 01:01:54.858
Do not be greedy, but be content.

20
01:02:01.858 --> 01:02:03.858
I rest my case.

21
01:02:05.858 --> 01:02:10.858
Do not be greedy, but be content with what you have.

22
01:02:10.858 --> 01:02:14.858
For God has said, I will never leave you.

23
01:02:14.858 --> 01:02:16.858
I will never forsake you.

24
01:02:17.858 --> 01:02:19.858
There is quite a bit here.

25
01:02:19.858 --> 01:02:27.858
And this goes quite against what the Western world around us proclaims.

26
01:02:27.858 --> 01:02:29.858
And tries to take us along with it.

27
01:02:29.858 --> 01:02:32.858
You often see this with the Bible, right?

28
01:02:32.858 --> 01:02:34.858
That it is radically different.

29
01:02:34.858 --> 01:02:37.858
And this is yet another good example of that.

30
01:02:38.858 --> 01:02:44.858
For the world around us keeps trying to drag us along.

31
01:02:44.858 --> 01:02:45.858
More, more, more.

32
01:02:45.858 --> 01:02:46.858
Have, have, have.

33
01:02:46.858 --> 01:02:48.858
Buy, buy, buy.

34
01:02:49.858 --> 01:02:52.858
Every year a new model of mobile phone, you know.

35
01:02:52.858 --> 01:02:53.858
Yes, I need to have that again.

36
01:02:53.858 --> 01:02:57.858
Not that anything has changed, but just a few millimeters.

37
01:02:57.858 --> 01:02:58.858
I need to have that.

38
01:02:58.858 --> 01:03:02.858
New television, new clothes, new car.

39
01:03:02.858 --> 01:03:06.858
Well, fundamentally there is nothing wrong with those things at all.

40
01:03:06.858 --> 01:03:12.858
But what is wrong is that the focus goes completely wrong because of this.

41
01:03:12.858 --> 01:03:16.858
This shifts our focus to me, me, me.

42
01:03:18.858 --> 01:03:22.858
Instead of building Jesus and his kingdom.

43
01:03:22.858 --> 01:03:33.858
And if you're not careful, you become increasingly focused on needing more money, a higher salary, a better job.

44
01:03:33.858 --> 01:03:35.858
I need to have it better, I need to have more.

45
01:03:35.858 --> 01:03:37.858
But all for you.

46
01:03:38.858 --> 01:03:40.858
Instead of for our kingdom.

47
01:03:41.858 --> 01:03:43.858
And that doesn't make you happy at all.

48
01:03:43.858 --> 01:03:48.858
Because you buy such a thing and it's fun for an hour or a day or a week.

49
01:03:48.858 --> 01:03:50.858
But then it passes again.

50
01:03:50.858 --> 01:03:55.858
It's just like that dopamine Tim talked about a few months ago.

51
01:03:55.858 --> 01:03:59.858
You get a kick from it, but it doesn't make you happy.

52
01:04:00.858 --> 01:04:03.858
But I know something that does make you happy.

53
01:04:03.858 --> 01:04:06.858
And that is building God's kingdom.

54
01:04:06.858 --> 01:04:13.858
But if you keep spending your money on things and wanting more while you actually don't need it.

55
01:04:13.858 --> 01:04:19.858
Then maybe very little or nothing is left to invest in God's kingdom.

56
01:04:21.858 --> 01:04:26.858
Have you ever thought about how happy you can be from buying something new?

57
01:04:27.858 --> 01:04:31.858
Or how happy you can be from building God's kingdom.

58
01:04:31.858 --> 01:04:33.858
Investing your money in the church.

59
01:04:33.858 --> 01:04:37.858
Ensuring that there is a larger hall so that more people can sit here.

60
01:04:37.858 --> 01:04:39.858
Do you also get a kick from that?

61
01:04:39.858 --> 01:04:45.858
Or is it that, that is quite a lot of money if you want to give tithes, for example.

62
01:04:46.858 --> 01:04:54.858
It's strange that you can get such a kick from buying something that you forget about shortly after.

63
01:04:54.858 --> 01:04:58.858
While you often don't get a kick from building God's kingdom.

64
01:04:58.858 --> 01:05:01.858
But building God's kingdom is worth everything.

65
01:05:01.858 --> 01:05:04.858
That's why I want to encourage you.

66
01:05:04.858 --> 01:05:08.858
Be careful with always wanting to have, have, have.

67
01:05:08.858 --> 01:05:10.858
Rather build God's kingdom.

68
01:05:10.858 --> 01:05:14.858
For that brings salvation for yourself and for the people around you.

69
01:05:22.858 --> 01:05:25.858
Hallelujah, are you ready for God's kingdom?

70
01:05:25.858 --> 01:05:27.858
Are you ready for God's kingdom?

71
01:05:28.858 --> 01:05:30.858
Thank you, band.

72
01:05:30.858 --> 01:05:32.858
For always doing this faithfully again.

73
01:05:32.858 --> 01:05:34.858
Hallelujah.

74
01:05:36.858 --> 01:05:38.858
Did you bring your Bible?

75
01:05:38.858 --> 01:05:40.858
Show it to me, if you happen to have it with you.

76
01:05:40.858 --> 01:05:41.858
Show it to me.

77
01:05:41.858 --> 01:05:44.858
Nice, nice.

78
01:05:44.858 --> 01:05:47.858
Who, who, who takes notes in their Bible?

79
01:05:47.858 --> 01:05:50.858
Who is such a Bible scribbler?

80
01:05:50.858 --> 01:05:52.858
Shame on you.

81
01:05:53.858 --> 01:05:57.858
Not me. Yes. No, not really.

82
01:05:57.858 --> 01:06:01.858
Yes, some really take very good notes.

83
01:06:01.858 --> 01:06:03.858
But you can also grab a notebook.

84
01:06:03.858 --> 01:06:06.858
We are really doing a Bible study.

85
01:06:06.858 --> 01:06:08.858
We started that last week.

86
01:06:08.858 --> 01:06:11.858
Last week was the introduction.

87
01:06:11.858 --> 01:06:17.858
That's always the case; when you buy a Bible study book, you always get an introduction.

88
01:06:17.858 --> 01:06:19.858
And then it leads in a little bit.

89
01:06:19.858 --> 01:06:20.858
What is this actually?

90
01:06:20.858 --> 01:06:22.858
What are we actually doing here?

91
01:06:22.858 --> 01:06:23.858
By whom was it written?

92
01:06:23.858 --> 01:06:25.858
When was it written?

93
01:06:25.858 --> 01:06:27.858
What was the historical background?

94
01:06:27.858 --> 01:06:29.858
What was the political background?

95
01:06:29.858 --> 01:06:31.858
What was the religious background?

96
01:06:31.858 --> 01:06:37.858
Those are very important questions you need to ask when doing a study of anything.

97
01:06:37.858 --> 01:06:42.858
But in the church, we come together to do Bible studies. Amen?

98
01:06:42.858 --> 01:06:44.858
Hallelujah.

99
01:06:45.858 --> 01:06:54.858
Dear King Jesus, I want to ask you to help us understand your Word, to grasp it.

100
01:06:54.858 --> 01:07:03.858
Lord, I want to ask you that if our hearts are hard to receive something from your Word,

101
01:07:03.858 --> 01:07:07.858
help us then, Lord, to receive it in faith.

102
01:07:07.858 --> 01:07:11.858
Holy Spirit, I want to ask you to warm our hearts.

103
01:07:11.858 --> 01:07:13.858
Lord, so that we can trust you.

104
01:07:13.858 --> 01:07:18.858
Lord, even in points of pain, even in points of struggle and disappointment,

105
01:07:18.858 --> 01:07:23.858
things that we find difficult in life or how we are set up as a person,

106
01:07:23.858 --> 01:07:27.858
Lord, I want to ask you to help us to embrace your Word.

107
01:07:27.858 --> 01:07:29.858
For your Word is the truth.

108
01:07:29.858 --> 01:07:31.858
Your Word gives life.

109
01:07:31.858 --> 01:07:33.858
Your Word gives eternal life.

110
01:07:33.858 --> 01:07:35.858
Your Word created heaven and earth.

111
01:07:35.858 --> 01:07:38.858
Your Word is creative and recreative.

112
01:07:39.858 --> 01:07:43.858
It is wonderful and ultimately gives ultimate peace.

113
01:07:43.858 --> 01:07:45.858
In Jesus' mighty name.

114
01:07:45.858 --> 01:07:47.858
And we all say amen.

115
01:07:47.858 --> 01:07:48.858
Amen.

116
01:07:49.858 --> 01:07:53.858
So we are doing a study on the chronicles.

117
01:07:53.858 --> 01:07:57.858
So come with me to the chronicles.

118
01:07:58.858 --> 01:08:01.858
And I actually say the chronicles on purpose.

119
01:08:01.858 --> 01:08:04.858
I actually prefer not to say first and second chronicles,

120
01:08:04.858 --> 01:08:08.858
for there is actually no first and second chronicles.

121
01:08:08.858 --> 01:08:11.858
The chronicles are simply the chronicles.

122
01:08:11.858 --> 01:08:13.858
Only because it was such a long story,

123
01:08:13.858 --> 01:08:18.858
and was written on one roll or one piece of material,

124
01:08:18.858 --> 01:08:20.858
and it was so large,

125
01:08:20.858 --> 01:08:23.858
they couldn't actually use this.

126
01:08:23.858 --> 01:08:25.858
So they just did an edit.

127
01:08:25.858 --> 01:08:27.858
They just cut it in half

128
01:08:27.858 --> 01:08:29.858
and you have first and second chronicles.

129
01:08:29.858 --> 01:08:32.858
So they are actually one and the same story.

130
01:08:32.858 --> 01:08:35.858
The chronicles means story.

131
01:08:35.858 --> 01:08:37.858
So chronicle means story.

132
01:08:37.858 --> 01:08:42.858
And so we are dealing here with the story of God's people.

133
01:08:42.858 --> 01:08:43.858
And this is important.

134
01:08:43.858 --> 01:08:45.858
And what I explained last week,

135
01:08:45.858 --> 01:08:52.858
is that you have the chronicles which stand in contrast to first and second kings.

136
01:08:52.858 --> 01:08:54.858
Actually, the stories are the same,

137
01:08:54.858 --> 01:08:57.858
and yet there is a big difference,

138
01:08:57.858 --> 01:09:04.858
because first and second kings were written before Israel was judged for their sin

139
01:09:04.858 --> 01:09:07.858
and taken away to a foreign land.

140
01:09:07.858 --> 01:09:13.858
So even before the exile, the story of the kings was central.

141
01:09:13.858 --> 01:09:17.858
And so you get the story of God's people in the kings,

142
01:09:17.858 --> 01:09:19.858
and then you see that this king did wrong,

143
01:09:19.858 --> 01:09:21.858
and that king did wrong,

144
01:09:21.858 --> 01:09:23.858
and that was a rotten man,

145
01:09:23.858 --> 01:09:25.858
and oh, it all went wrong.

146
01:09:25.858 --> 01:09:28.858
When you read two kings, you become more depressed than cheerful.

147
01:09:28.858 --> 01:09:33.858
And then comes that judgment and they are banished to a foreign land,

148
01:09:33.858 --> 01:09:35.858
and then they sit in that foreign land,

149
01:09:35.858 --> 01:09:39.858
and by God's grace there is at some point restoration.

150
01:09:39.858 --> 01:09:42.858
For God is indeed someone, and we talked about that last week,

151
01:09:42.858 --> 01:09:46.858
God is someone who judges our sin.

152
01:09:46.858 --> 01:09:48.858
And there are sanctions for that.

153
01:09:48.858 --> 01:09:50.858
Whether we like it or not,

154
01:09:50.858 --> 01:09:53.858
the Bible is full of these kinds of stories.

155
01:09:53.858 --> 01:09:55.858
So we cannot deny that God.

156
01:09:55.858 --> 01:09:59.858
We cannot say, yes, I do not believe in that God.

157
01:09:59.858 --> 01:10:01.858
Well, this is that God.

158
01:10:01.858 --> 01:10:04.858
This God rewards.

159
01:10:04.858 --> 01:10:07.858
This God protects.

160
01:10:07.858 --> 01:10:09.858
This God forgives.

161
01:10:09.858 --> 01:10:12.858
This God guides.

162
01:10:12.858 --> 01:10:14.858
This God gives sanctions.

163
01:10:14.858 --> 01:10:17.858
This God disciplines.

164
01:10:17.858 --> 01:10:20.858
This God can also put an end to something sometimes,

165
01:10:20.858 --> 01:10:22.858
and say, now it's completely over.

166
01:10:22.858 --> 01:10:25.858
This is this God.

167
01:10:25.858 --> 01:10:31.858
And what I also find important to say, by the way,

168
01:10:31.858 --> 01:10:38.858
is that it is not fair to want to box God into one this is God.

169
01:10:38.858 --> 01:10:41.858
That is not fair at all about a person.

170
01:10:41.858 --> 01:10:43.858
To say, this is God.

171
01:10:43.858 --> 01:10:47.858
It is not fair at all to say, well God is just this and that's it.

172
01:10:47.858 --> 01:10:49.858
So God always reacts like this.

173
01:10:49.858 --> 01:10:51.858
He has to react like this, because this is God.

174
01:10:51.858 --> 01:10:55.858
That would not be fair, because God is a person, just like you and me.

175
01:10:55.858 --> 01:10:59.858
Just a silly example, if you were to say, Tim is impatient,

176
01:10:59.858 --> 01:11:01.858
then everyone would say amen.

177
01:11:01.858 --> 01:11:03.858
Because then you say, Tim is impatient.

178
01:11:03.858 --> 01:11:07.858
But I was thinking about that, several times in my life,

179
01:11:07.858 --> 01:11:09.858
if I felt like thinking about it.

180
01:11:09.858 --> 01:11:13.858
But, Tim is impatient is not a fair statement about me,

181
01:11:13.858 --> 01:11:16.858
for on the other hand I have a lot of patience in other areas.

182
01:11:16.858 --> 01:11:20.858
I know about myself that I have a lot of patience with people.

183
01:11:20.858 --> 01:11:26.858
People can mess around and mess up and do foolish things and even hurt me and mess around,

184
01:11:26.858 --> 01:11:28.858
but I have a lot of patience for people.

185
01:11:28.858 --> 01:11:30.858
God has placed that in me.

186
01:11:30.858 --> 01:11:34.858
Every time I see someone messing around or sinning, I think to myself,

187
01:11:34.858 --> 01:11:39.858
yes foolish, but then I think to myself, as long as that person still has breath,

188
01:11:39.858 --> 01:11:43.858
there is a chance for him to return to the love of God.

189
01:11:43.858 --> 01:11:47.858
And I don't say that to boast, because when I am in a car

190
01:11:47.858 --> 01:11:51.858
and someone drives 70 on an 80 road, I do bite for lightning from heaven.

191
01:11:51.858 --> 01:11:53.858
So that is then again...

192
01:11:53.858 --> 01:11:56.858
So then I am indeed impatient.

193
01:11:56.858 --> 01:12:00.858
And then there is always a tractor suddenly driving in front of me from the right.

194
01:12:00.858 --> 01:12:04.858
And Vanessa always says, yes, that is the Lord.

195
01:12:06.858 --> 01:12:07.858
True or not, that is really it.

196
01:12:07.858 --> 01:12:11.858
There is always, always a tractor with a flat tire.

197
01:12:11.858 --> 01:12:14.858
Not normal. In reverse.

198
01:12:14.858 --> 01:12:17.858
It never happens to her, it always happens to me.

199
01:12:17.858 --> 01:12:21.858
So yes, I am impatient then.

200
01:12:21.858 --> 01:12:25.858
And yes, when I am working on a construction project with my friends from Open Church,

201
01:12:25.858 --> 01:12:28.858
I would have preferred to have it ready yesterday rather than tomorrow.

202
01:12:28.858 --> 01:12:31.858
So then the architect says, when do you want to start?

203
01:12:31.858 --> 01:12:33.858
Yes, yesterday, you know.

204
01:12:33.858 --> 01:12:36.858
And he also says, yes that's right, because tomorrow it will be much more expensive.

205
01:12:36.858 --> 01:12:38.858
He is right.

206
01:12:38.858 --> 01:12:40.858
So then I become impatient.

207
01:12:40.858 --> 01:12:44.858
When I am ambitious about something and when I am working on something.

208
01:12:44.858 --> 01:12:47.858
But I have many things in which I am very patient.

209
01:12:47.858 --> 01:12:50.858
When I am doing a task, I can actually be quite patient.

210
01:12:50.858 --> 01:12:54.858
When I am cooking nicely, I experience a lot of patience in that.

211
01:12:54.858 --> 01:12:57.858
When I have patience with people, then I have a lot of patience.

212
01:12:57.858 --> 01:13:04.858
Why? Because I have also been a pancake for so long, and I still am.

213
01:13:04.858 --> 01:13:07.858
God has grace and patience for me.

214
01:13:07.858 --> 01:13:09.858
And I feel that for my life.

215
01:13:09.858 --> 01:13:13.858
That he, thank you, for breaking the bread of your body.

216
01:13:13.858 --> 01:13:15.858
For spilling the wine of your blood.

217
01:13:15.858 --> 01:13:18.858
Thank you, Lord, that you have so much patience with me.

218
01:13:18.858 --> 01:13:20.858
And I also have patience with other people.

219
01:13:20.858 --> 01:13:24.858
So what I want to say is, it is not fair to say, Tim is this.

220
01:13:24.858 --> 01:13:29.858
And in the same way, it is also not fair to say about God, God always does this.

221
01:13:29.858 --> 01:13:31.858
That is not fair.

222
01:13:31.858 --> 01:13:35.858
Because God, and you discover this when you read the Bible.

223
01:13:35.858 --> 01:13:42.858
God acts according to His will, His character, and His truth.

224
01:13:42.858 --> 01:13:50.858
And in one story, you read about a God who is extremely gracious.

225
01:13:50.858 --> 01:13:55.858
And in another story, you read that God is very quickly done with someone.

226
01:13:55.858 --> 01:13:59.858
And He says to Pharaoh, you know what I'm going to do?

227
01:13:59.858 --> 01:14:04.858
I find you so annoying, He says to Pharaoh, that I will also harden your heart.

228
01:14:04.858 --> 01:14:06.858
So that you cannot obey me anymore.

229
01:14:06.858 --> 01:14:09.858
And then you read, wow, that is a harsh God.

230
01:14:09.858 --> 01:14:11.858
But God knows it.

231
01:14:11.858 --> 01:14:14.858
God knows it and He is God.

232
01:14:14.858 --> 01:14:20.858
And here is the thing, that is why we must trust Him.

233
01:14:20.858 --> 01:14:22.858
We just have to trust Him.

234
01:14:22.858 --> 01:14:26.858
We must trust Him that His will is the good will.

235
01:14:26.858 --> 01:14:29.858
And that His knowledge is the good knowledge.

236
01:14:29.858 --> 01:14:34.858
And that His, what do you call that in Dutch?

237
01:14:34.858 --> 01:14:36.858
Progressive insight.

238
01:14:36.858 --> 01:14:39.858
Evolving insight.

239
01:14:39.858 --> 01:14:41.858
What a language, huh?

240
01:14:41.858 --> 01:14:42.858
Evolving insight.

241
01:14:42.858 --> 01:14:43.858
He knows it.

242
01:14:43.858 --> 01:14:44.858
He is already there.

243
01:14:44.858 --> 01:14:47.858
He does not walk with us through life.

244
01:14:47.858 --> 01:14:48.858
I have explained that before, right?

245
01:14:48.858 --> 01:14:53.858
God is not very old that He started somewhere and walks with us in time.

246
01:14:53.858 --> 01:14:55.858
God stands above time.

247
01:14:55.858 --> 01:14:58.858
He governs the beginning and the end at the same moment.

248
01:14:58.858 --> 01:15:02.858
He is not subject to the law of time.

249
01:15:02.858 --> 01:15:06.858
So He created time but He is not in that time.

250
01:15:06.858 --> 01:15:08.858
He stands above that time because He made it.

251
01:15:08.858 --> 01:15:10.858
He stands above gravity.

252
01:15:10.858 --> 01:15:12.858
He stands above all the laws that He Himself has made.

253
01:15:12.858 --> 01:15:14.858
For He is not subordinate to those laws.

254
01:15:14.858 --> 01:15:17.858
So you are dealing with a God who encompasses everything.

